#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073558 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073879 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6e191386-9391-5e3c-9f2f-f17d55f9b6ca" :knowledge-point/title "Completing a Statement Describing a Ratio as a Fraction"}] :question/id #uuid "44e1e2da-6e2f-50b1-b982-dd5d4b5a432c" :question/math-academy-id "e-2265" :question/problem "What is missing in the following sentence?\n\nTo make a fertilizer Esther mixed $2$ quarts of fertilizer concentrate and $3$ quarts of distilled water, so there are ![](images/e6/e67bc79fa98ba44b9b1c5d5727182e936472f4b7d7b52967a54b069f178cf66d.svg) quarts of fertilizer concentrate for each quart of distilled water." :question/worked-solution "The ratio of the number of quarts of fertilizer concentrate to the number of quarts of distilled water is  ${\\color{blue}{2}}:{\\color{red}{3}}.$ \n\nWe can rewrite this ratio as a fraction, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{{\\color{blue}{2}}}{{\\color{red}{3}}}\n$$\n\nThis means that there is $\\dfrac{2}{3}$ quart of fertilizer concentrate for each quart of distilled water."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073559 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073880 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7435b531-e922-5db5-8140-463b7e66dd64" :knowledge-point/title "Completing a Statement by Interpreting a Fraction as a Ratio"}] :question/id #uuid "cd725418-654f-5cb2-a77a-9f6f9ed27825" :question/math-academy-id "e-2267" :question/problem "From left to right, what are the missing numbers in the following sentence?\n\nA chef requires $\\dfrac{1}{7}$ grams of chilies for each gram of turmeric for his recipe. Therefore, the recipe has a ratio of ![](images/ad/ada4a53796b76bbb852b81d98119a002b3840b7274b34aa8a321e1fe849215ee.svg) grams of chilies to ![](images/0c/0ce2b8005d66f823fc23dcefcbe5881d8a8fd85b34e2d711214b13ed959d85e8.svg) grams of turmeric." :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite the fraction $\\dfrac{1}{7}$ as a ratio:\n\n$$\n1:7\n$$\n\nTherefore, the recipe has a ratio of $1$ gram of chilies to $7$ grams of turmeric."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073658 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073786 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6a21dbe-0674-5fa2-b3ee-e4069115c6be" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Ratio as a Fraction"}] :question/id #uuid "b3b354ef-26fc-55dc-acdd-4b28c5f273ef" :question/math-academy-id "e-8139" :question/problem "What ratio describes the number of rhombuses to the number of triangles?\n\n![](images/49/49a799c1ec4b9e7caadd4af8714aa1133f33e7012b76083e9b241d05b0d2fee7.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we count the number of rhombuses. We see that there are $2$ rhombuses.\n\nThen, we count the number of triangles. We see that there are $3$ triangles.\n\nSo the ratio of rhombuses to triangles is $\\dfrac{2}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434586 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073786 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6a21dbe-0674-5fa2-b3ee-e4069115c6be" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Ratio as a Fraction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "299b2139-bac8-50da-ab9b-e8812d650ea2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434520} {:answer/id #uuid "2bb6155a-456c-5322-92a3-0e2a8239c88e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434521} {:answer/id #uuid "49058d3f-728b-5553-9d74-4fea29cd9c72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434526} {:answer/id #uuid "565c220f-57fb-578f-9ba9-34d4ef31ef23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434530} {:answer/id #uuid "ce37bf97-8187-55c5-b7b5-8f5eec74fa87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id 